---
import catalogue from "../../data/documentation.json";
const groups = [...new Set(catalogue.map((doc) => doc.group))];
---

<div class="workspace documentation">
  <header class="page-intro">
    <div class="eyebrow">PUBLIC DOCUMENTATION</div>
    <h1>How KEO works.<br />Where we go next.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Our evidence method, privacy rules, technical decisions and full
      application roadmap. Open to read, inspect and challenge.
    </p>
  </header>
  <div class="product-stages">
    <section class="panel">
      <span class="tag">MVP · KEO Light</span><h2>The ChatGPT Site.</h2><p>
        A lightweight evidence desk for phones, tablets and computers. Curated
        investigations, public sources, reference threats and county context,
        with paid AI disabled by default.
      </p><a href="/methodology/overview/">Read the project overview →</a>
    </section>
    <section class="panel future-stage">
      <span class="tag">PLANNED · AFTER PRODUCT HUNT</span><h2>
        The full web application.
      </h2><p>
        A shared evidence core with an optional 3D God’s Eye View. The light
        version, 2D map and list access remain part of the product; 3D is never
        required.
      </p><a href="/methodology/roadmap/">Explore the full roadmap →</a>
    </section>
  </div>
  <p class="notice">
    KEO is not an election authority. Missing evidence is not proof that a claim
    is false. The 3D workspace and live ingestion are planned, not available
    today.
  </p>
  <nav class="doc-jump-links" aria-label="Documentation sections">
    {
      groups.map((group, index) => (
        <a class="chip" href={"#docs-" + index}>
          {group}
        </a>
      ))
    }
  </nav>
  {
    groups.map((group, index) => (
      <section id={"docs-" + index} class="doc-section">
        <h2>{group}</h2>
        <div class="doc-grid">
          {catalogue
            .filter((doc) => doc.group === group)
            .map((doc) => (
              <a href={"/methodology/" + doc.slug + "/"} class="doc-card">
                <h3>
                  {doc.title}
                  <span aria-hidden="true"> ↗</span>
                </h3>
                <p>{doc.summary}</p>
              </a>
            ))}
        </div>
      </section>
    ))
  }
  <section class="panel" id="privacy">
    <h2>Your questions and images</h2><p>
      Results may be saved privately for a short period using native storage.
      Images are never automatically published. Read the full policy for
      consent, deletion and interrupted-request limits.
    </p><a href="/methodology/privacy/">Read privacy & retention →</a>
  </section>
  <p class="small muted">
    These pages are built from the same Markdown files as the GitHub repository.
    Code is MIT licensed; third-party data has separate terms.
  </p>
</div>
